  "intro": "The average value of $f$ on $[a,b]$ is $f_{\\text{avg}}=\\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx$, the constant height of a rectangle with the same area as under $f$. The Mean Value Theorem for Integrals guarantees a point $c$ in $(a,b)$ where $f(c)=f_{\\text{avg}}$, provided $f$ is continuous.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Find the average value of $f(x)=x^2$ on $[0,3]$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Use $f_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{3-0}\\int_0^3 x^2\\,dx$.",
          "$\\int_0^3 x^2\\,dx=\\frac{27}{3}=9$.",
          "Divide by the length $3$: $f_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{9}{3}=3$."
        ],
        "answer": "$f_{\\text{avg}}=3$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Find the $c$ guaranteed by the Mean Value Theorem for Integrals for $f(x)=x^2$ on $[0,3]$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "The average value is $3$, so set $f(c)=c^2=3$.",
          "Solve: $c=\\sqrt{3}\\approx 1.73$ (taking the value in $(0,3)$)."
        ],
        "answer": "$c=\\sqrt{3}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Find the average value of $f(x)=\\sin x$ on $[0,\\pi]$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$f_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{\\pi}\\int_0^\\pi \\sin x\\,dx$.",
          "$\\int_0^\\pi\\sin x\\,dx=2$.",
          "So $f_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{2}{\\pi}\\approx 0.637$."
        ],
        "answer": "$f_{\\text{avg}}=\\dfrac{2}{\\pi}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "Average value of $f(x)=x$ on $[0,4]$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$\\frac{1}{4}\\int_0^4 x\\,dx=\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8=2$."
        ],
        "answer": "$2$"
